/-!
# The sections of a coherent module over an affine chart form a finite module

Let `F` be an algebraic space and let `M` be a coherent `𝒪_F`-module on its small étale site.
Over an étale chart `V` whose underlying scheme is affine the sections `M(V)` form a **finite**
module over the ring `𝒪_F(V)` of regular functions on the chart.

Coherence only says that `M` is *locally* generated by finitely many sections, so the content is
an affine local-to-global step: quasi-compactness of the affine chart cuts the covering on which
generators exist down to a finite family of affine charts, the product of whose rings of
functions is faithfully flat over `𝒪_F(V)`, and faithfully flat descent turns local generation
into generation over the chart itself.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_of_locally_mem_span_restrict`: a section over an affine chart
  which lies locally in the span of the restrictions of a submodule of the sections already lies
  in that submodule.  This is the descent step.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.moduleFinite_sections_of_generates`: the sections over an affine chart
  carrying finitely many generators of `M` are spanned by those generators, hence form a finite
  module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.moduleFinite_sections_of_isFiniteType`: **the sections of a module of
  finite type which is cartesian on affine charts form a finite module over an affine chart.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.moduleFinite_sections_of_isCoherent` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.moduleFinite_sections_of_isNoetherianAffineChart`: **the sections of a
  coherent module over an affine chart, respectively over a Noetherian affine chart, form a
  finite module over the ring of the chart.**

## Implementation notes

Noetherianity of the ring of the chart is not used: finiteness of the sections comes from
coherence alone, exactly as on a scheme, where
`AlgebraicGeometry.moduleFinite_sections` derives it from quasi-coherence together with finite
type.  The Noetherian form is recorded because that is the shape in which the Artin–Rees
argument consumes it.

The descent step is run through a quotient.  For a submodule `N` of the sections over the affine
chart `A` and a section `t` lying, over each member `z` of a finite affine covering family of
`A`, in the `𝒪_F(z)`-span of the restrictions of `N`, injectivity of the base change comparison
of Stacks 03DX(2) over `z` turns `1 ⊗ t` into an element of `N.baseChange 𝒪_F(z)`, so the class
of `t` in `𝒪_F(z) ⊗ M(A)/N` vanishes; the classes over the members assemble into the class over
the product ring along the idempotents `Pi.single i 1`, whose sum is `1`, and faithful flatness
of the product kills it.  This is why the whole family, rather than one member at a time, is
needed: no single member of an étale covering family is surjective.

The base change property of the sections is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsCartesianOnAffineCharts`,
which for a quasi-coherent module is Descent, Proposition 03DX(2)
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`); the finiteness
results below therefore carry no `@[stacks]` attribute of their own.

